       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 30 mg daily is three times the usual maximum dose of 10 mg once daily. At that dose there's a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. Overdoses of this size have caused shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema. Normal renal and hepatic function doesn't change that.\n\nCould you confirm what you intended? Some possibilities:\n- **10 mg once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n- **5 mg once daily**, the usual starting dose. Some patients, such as older adults or those with hepatic impairment, start at 2.5 mg.\n- **A different drug or dose**, if 30 mg was meant for something else, for example a different agent or a typo for 3.0 or 10 mg.\n\nIf you do want 30 mg, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional and above the labeled maximum. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
